35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The diaries show six weeks lost to weather. That is a huge chunk of the year.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"My data is shocking. Specialist rooms sit empty, but general rooms are always full.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,I found the technicians have spare hours. We can use them to fix the manual routines.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,The ratings confirm my fear. Projects that only helped one wing were rated poorly.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The tenders show a twenty percent jump in plant costs. The reserves are empty.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, if the reserves are empty, how do we pay for the weather delays?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, that matches what I see. The general rooms are the ones people actually need.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Shizue, we can use the spare technician hours to handle the manual checks faster.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Yumi, exactly. We need spaces that everyone can use, not just a few.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shizue, we don't. We just get hit with the full market price every time.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,That is terrifying. We need a plan that is quick to finish and low risk.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,I agree. We should focus on the general rooms. They are the bottleneck.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"I support that. If we automate the manual checks, the technicians can handle the general rooms better.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,I am with you. High utility and accessibility are the only way to get good ratings.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I concur. A simple, general-purpose upgrade avoids the expensive, volatile plant costs.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,It seems we are all leaning toward the general room upgrade. It is safer for the timeline.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,It is also the kindest choice for the students and staff who are always waiting.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,It is the only choice that respects the staff we actually have.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,It is the choice that will actually be used and appreciated. I am confident in this.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,It is the only choice that does not bleed money into the void. I am in.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
